---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="AI Search Optimization & AEO Services | Kelp"
  description="Prepare your website for AI-driven discovery with a practical audit and improvements to crawl access, content, structure, and measurement."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="AI Services"
    title="AI Search Optimization Built on a Website Worth Recommending"
    description="People now ask AI tools to compare services, explain products, and suggest businesses. Your site needs to give those systems—and the people who follow their links—clear, accurate reasons to understand your offer. Kelp helps businesses improve the foundations for AI-driven discovery while making the website more useful to customers."
    lottieFile="ai-search-optimization.json"
  />
  <section class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where Teams Get Stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Many businesses have useful expertise that their website barely
        explains. Key pages may be difficult to crawl, service descriptions may
        be vague, and proof may be scattered across channels. In AI search, that
        creates a weak source for both an answer system and the person who
        follows its link.
      </p>
      <h2>How We Fix It</h2>
      <p>
        We examine the questions customers ask, the pages that should answer
        them, crawler access, internal structure, and evidence of real work.
        Then we prioritize content and technical changes. We review results as a
        pattern across referrals, landing pages, and qualified outcomes rather
        than treating one generated answer as a fixed ranking.
      </p>
      <h2>What AI Search Readiness Actually Involves</h2>
      <p>
        There is no single AEO tag or prompt that guarantees a recommendation.
        For Google AI features, Google says ordinary SEO fundamentals still
        apply. For ChatGPT search, OpenAI says a public site can appear and
        advises publishers to allow OAI-SearchBot if they want content eligible
        for summaries and snippets. The work starts with access, helpful
        content, and credible evidence rather than a claim that anyone can
        control a generated answer.
      </p>
      <p>
        We review whether important pages can be crawled and indexed, whether
        the business and services are described plainly, and whether content
        answers the questions buyers really ask. We look at internal links, page
        structure, schema where appropriate, and consistency between website
        claims and other public information. A useful product or service page
        should explain fit, process, specifications, limitations, and next
        steps.
      </p>
      <h2>From Audit to Implementation</h2>
      <p>
        Kelp can turn findings into a prioritized plan for content, design,
        development, and measurement. That may include rewriting thin service
        pages, clarifying product information, repairing technical barriers,
        adding evidence from real work, or improving the path from an AI
        referral to an enquiry or purchase. We measure qualified traffic and
        outcomes alongside visibility observations; individual AI answers can
        vary by query and context.
      </p>
      <h2>Start with the Free Scan</h2>
      <p>
        Kelp's <a href="/website-checker/">Website Checker</a> gives a quick
        report covering AI search readiness, technical and local SEO, broken
        links, schema, and conversion opportunities. It is a starting point, not
        a complete strategy. A deeper engagement examines the pages, customer
        questions, competitors, and business outcomes behind the report.
      </p>
      <h3 class="h4">Can Kelp guarantee that ChatGPT recommends us?</h3>
      <p>
        No. No agency controls which businesses an AI system mentions. Kelp can
        improve the accessibility, clarity, accuracy, and usefulness of the
        information those systems may encounter.
      </p>
      <h3 class="h4">Is AI search optimization separate from SEO?</h3>
      <p>
        It builds on SEO, content strategy, and website quality. Google states
        that its AI search features do not require a special file or markup. The
        exact tactics depend on the platform and the customer question.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your leads are changing and you need to know whether your site is
        prepared, talk with Kelp about an AI search readiness plan.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>AI search readiness and content audit</li>
        <li>Technical access and page-structure review</li>
        <li>Service or product content improvements</li>
        <li>Measurement and ongoing refinement plan</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Start with the <a href="/website-checker/">Website Checker</a> report
        and a shortlist of the services or products most important to the
        business. We can then define a deeper audit and implementation plan
        around those pages.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3 class="h4">
        Is there a special file that makes AI tools recommend us?
      </h3>
      <p>
        No. Google says its AI features use ordinary SEO foundations, and OpenAI
        describes crawler access as one eligibility factor. Relevance and useful
        information still matter.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Your Project
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
